<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria M1 rises 8.39 pct, M2 up 3.86 pct in week.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria M1 rises 8.39 pct, M2 up 3.86 pct in week.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgarian M1 money supply rose to 1.275 trillion  levs on July 25 from 1.176 trillion levs a week earlier and M2 increased  to 4.552 trillion levs from 4.383 trillion levs, preliminary central  bank figures showed.</p>
<p>Total broad money rose 3.47 percent to 4.771 trillion levs in the  week to July 25.</p>
<p>Conversion of foreign currency-denominated deposits into levs was  made at the central bank fixing of 1,000 levs per mark for July 25,  July 18 and July 11.</p>
<p>The lev was pegged at 1,000 per mark on July 1 under an IMF-prescribed  fixed exchange rate mechanism, known as a currency board.</p>
<p>The system requires levs in circulation to be fully matched</p>
<p>by central bank foreign exchange reserves.</p>
